Environmental memory

Reconstruct historical environmental changes from tree rings, corals, and other physical archives.

Eventually we could follow one phenomenon across multiple substrates: how environmental change affected organisms, how organisms changed ecosystems, how ecosystems shaped human settlement, and how humans remembered those changes.

That’s when the Stereoscope becomes a genuine cross-domain discovery instrument.

